# Line endings must not depend on the platform.
#
# conformance/golden/*.txt is compared to rendered output byte for byte, and
# the renderer emits "\n" everywhere. A CRLF checkout — which is what Windows
# gets by default — fails every conformance case in every binding at once, and
# makes gofmt reject every .go file. Forcing LF is what keeps the "all seven
# languages produce identical bytes" guarantee true on Windows too.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The goldens carry raw ANSI escape sequences and exist to be compared as
# bytes: never let any normalization touch them.
conformance/golden/*.txt -text

# Generated: the base64-encoded WebAssembly module.
bindings/js/src/wasm-binary.js -diff
